],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'Add InFlightGauge.hold(), which counts accepted background work and returns an idempotent release.'","'wait_for_idle(gauge) ... so mcp_server.main()'s binding.cleanup() happens only after in-flight work ends'","ABSENCE: the plan states hold-before-start ordering and idempotent release but does not state the counter increment/decrement and the drain's zero-check are themselves atomic under concurrent AnyIO-worker + daemon-thread mutation."],"finding":"The InFlightGauge counter is mutated concurrently (AnyIO request workers incrementing/decrementing on accept/complete, plus spawn_context_daemon threads taking/releasing holds, plus the SIGTERM drain reading the count to decide should_exit), but the plan does not state that the counter mutation itself is atomic / lock-protected. The plan establishes the hold-before-start ORDERING (so a tool never returns to 0 before its daemon is counted) and an idempotent release, but ordering does not by itself guarantee a race-free read-modify-write of the shared count, nor a race-free drain read of 'in flight == 0'.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f80bd053adcc14caf","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 (InFlightGauge.hold / DRAINED_TOOLS gauge) and step 3 (wait_for_idle)","norm_id":"ne3f9c792aa14f190","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two spawn_context_daemon calls (e.g. verify_completion_start + review_plan_start) take holds concurrently; an unsynchronized read-modify-write on the count loses an increment, so the drain sees 0 while a daemon still holds the key — the exact forced-close race the plan is closing.","The drain thread reads count==0 between a decrement and the next request's increment and sets should_exit, cutting a just-accepted signing tool."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify a threading.Lock (or asyncio-safe equivalent bridged for the daemon threads) guarding th